item.text:
Exposure assessment for 2022: `limited_exposure_with_choices`. Tshisekedi had no nuclear arsenal or nuclear command-and-control to manage, but he did make some ruler-level choices in disarmament, cyber governance, and crisis de-escalation. I screened roughly 30 documents and kept the narrow set that actually bears on 1B.

**Reused evidence**
- None. There were no previously accepted web evidence items to reuse.

**New evidence**
- Office identity and tenure.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Félix-Antoine Tshisekedi Tshilombo - Présidence RDC","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/president/le-president","claim":"The official bio states that Félix-Antoine Tshisekedi Tshilombo has been President of the Republic since 24 January 2019 and was elected on 30 December 2018.","locator":"bio intro paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential biography; direct office-identification source.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct office confirmation for the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Official self-description of the office holder; useful for identity and tenure only.","contrary_evidence":["Self-published and favorable; not independent verification of performance."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Constitutional authority and constraints.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Constitution","publisher":"Leganet","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://www.leganet.cd/Legislation/Constitution.htm","claim":"The constitutional text makes the president commander-in-chief, chair of the defense council, and the official who may proclaim a state of siege after consultation; it also requires cabinet, defense-council, and parliamentary authorization for declaring war.","locator":"Search result snippet for Articles 81, 83, 85, 86","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary constitutional text; directly states the ruler's formal security powers and limits.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"This was the governing constitutional frame in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Formal office authority, not proof of how Tshisekedi personally exercised it.","contrary_evidence":["Legal authority does not prove effective or prudent use in practice."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.3","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- TPNW ratification date.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons status table","publisher":"United Nations Treaty Collection","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://treaties.un.org/Pages/ViewDetails.aspx?chapter=26&clang=_en&mtdsg_no=XXVI-9&src=IND","claim":"The treaty status table records the Democratic Republic of the Congo as having signed the TPNW on 20 September 2017 and ratified it on 22 September 2022.","locator":"rows for Democratic Republic of the Congo in the TPNW status table","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN depositary record with the treaty action date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 treaty action.","ruler_attribution":"State action during Tshisekedi's presidency; not a personal safety-performance measure.","contrary_evidence":["Ratification is a commitment, not evidence of full implementation."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}

- 2022 disarmament summary.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNODA 2022 Yearbook, Chapter 1","publisher":"United Nations Office for Disarmament Affairs","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://yearbook-archive.unoda.org/2022/chapter1.html","claim":"The yearbook summary states that in 2022 nine states ratified the Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons, including the Democratic Republic of the Congo.","locator":"TPNW signature and ratification section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNODA yearbook summary of 2022 treaty actions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 year summary.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level treaty action under Tshisekedi's presidency.","contrary_evidence":["Still a treaty-summary source, not proof of domestic implementation or safety governance."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}

- IAEA safeguards baseline.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List: Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IAEA Office of Legal Affairs","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=CD","claim":"The IAEA country sheet shows an in-force safeguards agreement in connection with the NPT and an additional protocol for the Democratic Republic of the Congo.","locator":"Safeguards Agreements section, lines 112-124","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary IAEA country fact sheet with treaty/safeguards status.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Enduring nonproliferation baseline in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Structural national safeguards context; not a ruler-specific action record.","contrary_evidence":["Safeguards status does not show how safely any domestic institutions were run in 2022."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.9"]}

- Cyber strategy created under presidential impulse.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"La Stratégie nationale de cybersécurité","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2023-06-23","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/la_strategie_nationale_de_cybersecurite","claim":"The presidency says the National Cybersecurity Strategy 2022-2025 was produced by experts convened by a technical commission created by the presidential cabinet under Tshisekedi's impulse, and that the strategy was validated by the president after work carried out from February to July 2022.","locator":"lines 72-76","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential publication describing the strategy's creation and validation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Built from 2022 work and published as the 2022-2025 national strategy.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential validation of a cyber-risk governance instrument.","contrary_evidence":["Published after the 2022 period; it reflects 2022 drafting and validation rather than full implementation."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}

- Cyber governance and Malabo ratification push.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la soixante-treizième réunion du Conseil des Ministres","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-10-16","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_soixante-treizieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"At the 14 October 2022 Council of Ministers meeting chaired by Tshisekedi, the president urged the government to pursue ratification of the AU Convention on Cybersecurity and Personal Data Protection (Malabo) and said effective cybercrime response required a rigorous legal corpus.","locator":"lines 72 and 100-102","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government record of a chaired council meeting and the president's stated priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 policy choice.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler-attributed governance choice over cyber policy.","contrary_evidence":["This is a policy directive, not evidence that the agency or legal reforms were actually implemented in 2022."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}

- Independent policy corroboration on cyber infrastructure.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Cybersecurity Strategy for 2022-2025","publisher":"IEA","publication_date":"2026-04-27","url":"https://www.iea.org/policies/30396-national-cybersecurity-strategy-for-2022-2025","claim":"The policy database records the DRC's National Cybersecurity Strategy for 2022-2025 as in force and says it protects electricity, petroleum, and gas subsectors as activities of vital importance.","locator":"policy summary and lines 213-228","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent database entry, but derivative rather than original government text.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Summarizes the 2022 national cyber policy environment.","ruler_attribution":"State-level policy context rather than a direct ruler statement.","contrary_evidence":["Derivative database entry; weaker than the original presidential source."],"lenses":["1B.9","1B.10"]}

- Atomic-energy appointment.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"sommaire JO n° 14 15.07.2022","publisher":"Leganet Journal Officiel","publication_date":"2022-07-15","url":"https://www.leganet.cd/Legislation/JO/2022/sommaire.15.07.2022.html","claim":"The official journal summary records Ordinance No. 22/066 of 22 June 2022 appointing a Commissioner General to the Atomic Energy Commission.","locator":"journal summary entry for 22 June 2022","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Official journal summary, but only a catalog entry and not the full ordinance text in the retrieved snippet.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 administrative action.","ruler_attribution":"Shows presidential appointment authority in a sensitive atomic-energy domain; it does not prove safety performance.","contrary_evidence":["Appointment alone does not show risk-reducing competence, safety safeguards, or any nuclear-relevant outcome."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9"]}

- Eastern crisis and displacement.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adresse à la nation du Président de la République, Félix Tshisekedi suite à la détérioration de la situation sécuritaire à l’est du pays","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/adresse_a_la_nation_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_suite_a_la_deterioration_de_la_situation_securitaire_a_lest_du_pays","claim":"Tshisekedi said the M23 crisis in North Kivu was being carried out with Rwandan support and that more than 200,000 people had fled, then said he had instructed the government to organize assistance.","locator":"lines 77-78","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential address with explicit crisis framing and response instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 crisis response.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement and crisis directive.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is self-justifying and the attribution of external support is contested in the wider information environment."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Peace-process appeal.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : Félix Tshisekedi réitère son appel aux groupes armés à rejoindre le processus de paix","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-05-28","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/05/28/actualite/securite/rdc-felix-tshisekedi-reitere-son-appel-aux-groupes-armes-rejoindre-le","claim":"Radio Okapi reports that, during the 55th Council of Ministers meeting, Tshisekedi reiterated an unconditional call for armed groups to join the peace process and condemned the M23's breach of the republican commitment.","locator":"line 147","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent local reporting with a clear attributed ruler action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 peace-process conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the president's communication in cabinet.","contrary_evidence":["The source reports rhetoric and process, not a verified cessation of violence."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Nairobi process as inclusive disarmament track.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC-Sécurité: Les nations Unies saluent l'orientation donnée au processus de Nairobi et insiste sur un dialogue continu, franc et ouvert entre toutes les parties prenantes régionales","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-05-05","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/05/05/rdc-securite-les-nations-unies-saluent-lorientation-donnee-au-processus-de-nairobi-et","claim":"The article says the UN welcomed the Nairobi consultations led by the presidency as an inclusive consultation with armed groups to identify measures needed for voluntary disarmament.","locator":"lines 99-100","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local media quoting UN and presidential-process framing with clear date and attribution.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 peace-process context.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect ruler attribution through his emissaries and the presidency-led process.","contrary_evidence":["The piece reflects process endorsement, not evidence that Tshisekedi personally reduced risk beyond opening talks."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Nairobi first-stage consultations.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : fin de la première étape du dialogue consultatif de Nairobi entre le gouvernement et les groupes armés","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-04-28","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/04/28/rdc-fin-de-la-premiere-etape-du-dialogue-consultatif-de-nairobi-entre-le-gouvernement-et","claim":"The first stage of the Nairobi dialogue ended after five days, with nearly 30 delegates from armed groups participating and observers from Rwanda, Uganda, Burundi, the UN, CIRGL, the United States, and France present.","locator":"lines 84-87","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed local reporting with specific participants and observers.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 de-escalation context.","ruler_attribution":"Shows the president's emissaries operating in a multilateral peace track.","contrary_evidence":["Consultation is not the same as durable de-escalation or implementation."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Nairobi III ceasefire conditions.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Troisième phase des pourparlers de Nairobi : Les chefs d’Etats appellent les groupes armés à déposer les armes","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/11/29/emissions/dialogue-entre-congolais/troisieme-phase-des-pourparlers-de-nairobi-les-chefs","claim":"Tshisekedi said the M23 must cease hostilities, withdraw from occupied positions, and return to its November 2021 positions as the condition for joining the Nairobi process.","locator":"line 147","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent local radio coverage with an attributed presidential statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 crisis-management position.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement in a crisis and negotiation setting.","contrary_evidence":["The hard-line conditions may slow negotiations, even if they also set de-escalation terms."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Humanitarian scale of the inherited crisis.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNHCR deeply concerned by renewed violence displacing thousands in North Kivu, DR Congo","publisher":"UNHCR","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/news/briefing-notes/unhcr-deeply-concerned-renewed-violence-displacing-thousands-north-kivu-dr","claim":"UNHCR said more than 72,000 people had been displaced by fighting in recent days in North Kivu province.","locator":"lines 392-392","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN humanitarian briefing note with a specific displacement count.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 crisis baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited humanitarian emergency rather than a ruler-specific safety choice.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian severity alone does not distinguish Tshisekedi's own contribution from inherited conflict dynamics."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Year-end displacement baseline.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo situation","publisher":"UNHCR Global Focus","publication_date":"2023-06-14","url":"https://reporting.unhcr.org/democratic-republic-congo-situation-global-report-2022","claim":"UNHCR's 2022 global report says insecurity in eastern provinces displaced hundreds of thousands in 2022 and that the DRC ended 2022 with 5.5 million internally displaced people.","locator":"2022 situation overview and 2022 year-end population figures","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UNHCR year-end summary with concrete displacement totals.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 end-state summary.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited state-of-affairs context, not direct ruler attribution.","contrary_evidence":["Retrospective summary; not a direct contemporaneous policy record."],"lenses":["1B.10","1B.8"]}

- Rebel violence and civilian killings.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Resurgent M23 Rebels Target Civilians","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-07-25","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/07/25/dr-congo-resurgent-m23-rebels-target-civilians","claim":"Human Rights Watch said the M23 summarily killed at least 29 civilians since mid-June 2022 and warned of possible Rwandan support for the group.","locator":"lines 607-608","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable rights-monitoring report with a precise casualty claim and date.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact 2022 violence context.","ruler_attribution":"Shows the violent environment Tshisekedi was responding to; the killings are attributable to the rebel group, not directly to him.","contrary_evidence":["The report is adversarial to the rebel group; the Rwandan-support allegation is framed as concern rather than conclusively proven fact."],"lenses":["1B.8","1B.10"]}

- Tshisekedi's UNGA framing of aggression and overtures.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Félix Tshisekedi: « En dépit de ma bonne volonté (…) certains de nos voisins n’ont trouvé mieux que de nous remercier par l’agression »","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/09/21/felix-tshisekedi-en-depit-de-ma-bonne-volonte-certains-de-nos-voisins-nont-trouve-mieux","claim":"Reporting on Tshisekedi's UN General Assembly speech says he told the world that, despite his goodwill and peace overtures, some neighbors responded with aggression and support for armed groups.","locator":"lines 94-95","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Local reporting on a clearly dated presidential speech with direct quotations and attributed framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 international crisis diplomacy.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler rhetoric in a crisis context.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is self-justifying and its external-attribution claims are contested in the broader record."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I screened official constitutional and treaty records, presidency pages, UN/IAEA material, local-language media, humanitarian reporting, and rights monitoring.
- Kept because they were directly useful: UN Treaty Collection, IAEA country sheet, presidency bio, presidency council minutes, presidency address, Radio Okapi, Actualite.cd, UNHCR, HRW, UNODA yearbook, IEA policy page.
- Rejected as duplicate or weak: the ICAN DRC page, because it mainly restates the treaty action already captured by the UN Treaty Collection and adds later NGO synthesis; Reuters/AP/BBC-style searches did not surface a cleaner, more material 1B-specific source in the available results.
- Rejected as wrong-country / not usable for DRC: the UNODA spotlight titled "Congo ratifies the TPNW" referred to Congo rather than the Democratic Republic of the Congo, so I did not use it.
- Rejected as off-target: broad conflict, governance, and humanitarian items that did not add anything beyond the kept UNHCR/HRW/press sources.
- Blocked/partially blocked: the Leganet constitution page timed out on direct open, so I relied on the search-result snippet for the constitutional text and did not over-chase it.

**Remaining gaps**
- No direct evidence of nuclear command-and-control, custody, accident-prevention, or safety-safeguard reforms under Tshisekedi in 2022.
- No direct evidence of nuclear-rhetoric management, because the DRC is non-nuclear and the 2022 record is mostly about disarmament accession and crisis diplomacy.
- No material evidence on biology/AI/existential-risk governance beyond the cyber strategy and Malabo push.
- The chapter is still thin on ruler-specific risk-reduction outcomes versus policy intent. More search would help only if you want to push beyond a cautious `limited_exposure_with_choices` evidence assessment toward a tighter judgment of 1B.8-1B.10.
